{"title":"Topicwise Test-4 Part Syllabus GATE 2026 EE Control Systems-2","fileName":"088_Topicwise Test-4 Part Syllabus GATE 2026 EE Control Systems-2.html","branch":"ELECTRICAL ENGINEERING","series":"GATE 2026 + GATE 2025 Online Test Series Electrical Engineering","provider":"MADE EASY","duration":2700,"questions":[{"qnum":1,"type":"NAT","correct":"","right":2,"wrong":0,"qtext":"<p>The gain margin in dB of the unity feedback control system with transfer function.</p>\n<p><img src=\"/media/a1d054e0711785f07cae7e9ae8ea0309635795f5.png\" align=\"absmiddle\" loading=\"lazy\" /> is ________ dB. (Answer upto two decimal places)</p></div>\n<div><span>NAT</span>","options":[],"nat":{"low":"-4.437","high":"-4.437"},"solution":"<p>-4.437 (-4.450 - -4.41)</p>\n<div> </div>\n<div>\n<div> </div>\n<div><img src=\"/media/d16309e923e21449521d24fd1efd7599bef4b130.png\" loading=\"lazy\" /></div>\n</div>\n<div> </div>","subject":"Technical"},{"qnum":2,"type":"NAT","correct":"","right":2,"wrong":0,"qtext":"<p>The number of encirclements in clockwise direction of the point –1 + <em>j</em>0, in the <em>G</em>(<em>s</em>)<em>H</em>(<em>s</em>) plane, for<br />\nthe system having its open-loop transfer function <em>G</em>(<em>s</em>) <em>H</em>(<em>s</em>) = <img src=\"/media/1c2495a6fbc7f874892a46d1b4f51952b9c8a9c5.png\" align=\"absmiddle\" loading=\"lazy\" /> is _______ .</p></div>\n<div><span>NAT</span>","options":[],"nat":{"low":"2","high":"2"},"solution":"<p>2</p>\n<div> </div>\n<div><img src=\"/media/2628068ffdb3aa494b2abd5f16e948aeeeb479da.png\" loading=\"lazy\" /></div>","subject":"Technical"},{"qnum":3,"type":"NAT","correct":"","right":2,"wrong":0,"qtext":"<p>Consider the feedback system shown:</p>\n<div> </div>\n<div><img src=\"/media/0d0f75d905fc24e2c94a84f5cf9fe4a51c2adf6a.png\" loading=\"lazy\" /></div>\n<div> </div>\n<div>If the resonant peak and resonant frequency of this system is 1.04 and 11.55 rad/sec respectively, then bandwidth is ________ rad/sec. (Answer upto two decimal places)</div></div>\n<div><span>NAT</span>","options":[],"nat":{"low":"25.41","high":"25.41"},"solution":"<p>25.41 (25.00 - 26.00)</p>\n<div> </div>\n<div><img src=\"/media/3e3125f15d58f4210292355f0b54887469f4daba.png\" loading=\"lazy\" /></div>","subject":"Technical"},{"qnum":4,"type":"MCQ","correct":"B","right":2,"wrong":0.66,"qtext":"<p>The open-loop transfer function of a unity feedback system is given by <img src=\"/media/ba9cea9adf2894f943831c67b6f0df33507af28f.png\" align=\"absmiddle\" loading=\"lazy\" /> Phase margin for K = 1, <em>T</em><sub>1</sub> = 0.2 and <em>T</em><sub>2</sub> = 0.05 is _______</p>","options":[{"letter":"A","text":"<div> 103.80°</div>","isCorrect":false},{"letter":"B","text":"<div> 76.2°</div>","isCorrect":true},{"letter":"C","text":"<div> 101.2°</div>","isCorrect":false},{"letter":"D","text":"<div> 78.2°</div>","isCorrect":false}],"nat":{"low":"","high":""},"solution":"<p>(b)</p>\n<div> </div>\n<div><img src=\"/media/d2cc284606199a7c9e89652a3c5a84e17a9a558c.png\" loading=\"lazy\" /></div>\n<div><img src=\"/media/09e0016146fbeb330884b4e00714e69adff87bd1.png\" loading=\"lazy\" /></div>","subject":"Technical"},{"qnum":5,"type":"MCQ","correct":"C","right":1,"wrong":0.33,"qtext":"<p>A system is described by the state equations <img src=\"/media/d841c4e5c73f7682c5cc0ebff0bd9fe9c812eba5.png\" align=\"absmiddle\" loading=\"lazy\" /> Which of the following option is correct?</p>","options":[{"letter":"A","text":"<div> Given system is controllable but not observable.</div>","isCorrect":false},{"letter":"B","text":"<div> Given system is observable but not controllable.</div>","isCorrect":false},{"letter":"C","text":"<div> Given system is controllable and observable both.</div>","isCorrect":true},{"letter":"D","text":"<div> Given system is neither controllable nor observable.</div>","isCorrect":false}],"nat":{"low":"","high":""},"solution":"<p>(c)</p>\n<div> </div>\n<div><img src=\"/media/cd03da9e396ee24d5a1d01d5027f02a6388adc72.png\" loadin