/div>","subject":"Technical"},{"qnum":10,"type":"NAT","correct":"","right":1,"wrong":0,"qtext":"<p>The transfer function of a system is:</p>\n<div> </div>\n<div><img src=\"/media/d8b9c78bb6ecd7233c25187c75a19746fc6ccaae.png\" loading=\"lazy\" /></div>\n<div> </div>\n<div>In the state-space representation of the system, the minimum number of state variables (in integer) necessary is _______ .</div></div>\n<div><span>NAT</span>","options":[],"nat":{"low":"3","high":"3"},"solution":"<p>3</p>\n<div> </div>\n<div><img src=\"/media/00ffc467bab2548b593f46b843182c7da4ca4aad.png\" loading=\"lazy\" /></div>","subject":"Technical"},{"qnum":11,"type":"MCQ","correct":"A","right":1,"wrong":0.33,"qtext":"<p>A unity feedback system has the following open loop frequency response:</p>\n<div> </div>\n<div><img src=\"/media/19ebc36d8df1204caace55d5130df4baa1e47ec0.png\" loading=\"lazy\" /></div>\n<div>The gain and phase margin of the system are</div>","options":[{"letter":"A","text":"<div> 2.5 dB and 5°</div>","isCorrect":true},{"letter":"B","text":"<div> 5 dB and 10°</div>","isCorrect":false},{"letter":"C","text":"<div> 7.5 dB and 15°</div>","isCorrect":false},{"letter":"D","text":"<div> 10 dB and 20°</div>","isCorrect":false}],"nat":{"low":"","high":""},"solution":"<p>(a)</p>\n<div> </div>\n<div><img src=\"/media/8aebad6727fb4175d660a4a27687f85f02cc37b6.png\" loading=\"lazy\" /></div>","subject":"Technical"},{"qnum":12,"type":"NAT","correct":"A","right":1,"wrong":0,"qtext":"<p>The input <img src=\"/media/c7f213e8f006008d2fad0580ef229b6c4b3b0ee0.png\" align=\"absmiddle\" loading=\"lazy\" /> is applied to a system whose transfer function <img src=\"/media/45671646c41ce9c1f81dd5c1c9c0e32f813c6f2a.png\" align=\"absmiddle\" loading=\"lazy\" /> The amplitude of the output of the system is ________ . (Answer upto three decimal places)</p></div>\n<div><span>NAT</span>","options":[],"nat":{"low":"0.08","high":"0.08"},"solution":"<p>0.08 (0.07 - 0.09)</p>\n<div> </div>\n<div><img src=\"/media/3ffaca7ef8647888a09837bf57cf4521b1e4e12b.png\" loading=\"lazy\" /></div>\n<div> </div>","subject":"Technical"},{"qnum":13,"type":"MSQ","correct":"A,B","right":1,"wrong":0,"qtext":"<p>In a unity-gain feedback control system, the plant <em>P</em>(<em>s</em>) = <img src=\"/media/2f273129d66dfe1e45cc2ae568a7b98d398a4dee.png\" align=\"absmiddle\" loading=\"lazy\" /> is controlled by a lag compensator <em>C</em>(<em>s</em>) = <img src=\"/media/d77c2423b6b2ae717a703dc51318a80464c13878.png\" align=\"absmiddle\" loading=\"lazy\" /> If the slope of the asymptotic bode magnitude plot of the loop gain at ω = 3 rad/sec is –60 dB/decades then the possible value of a is</p>","options":[{"letter":"A","text":"<div> 10</div>","isCorrect":true},{"letter":"B","text":"<div> 4</div>","isCorrect":true},{"letter":"C","text":"<div> 1000</div>","isCorrect":false},{"letter":"D","text":"<div> 10000</div>","isCorrect":false}],"nat":{"low":"","high":""},"solution":"<p>(a, b)</p>\n<div> </div>\n<div><img src=\"/media/76a34d371c1988880d3ffae0e5df0bf746fc2780.png\" loading=\"lazy\" /></div>","subject":"Technical"},{"qnum":14,"type":"MCQ","correct":"C","right":1,"wrong":0.33,"qtext":"<p>Polar plot of a system at ω<sub>pc</sub> = 4 rad/sec gives <em>G</em>(ω<em><sub>pc</sub></em>)<em>H</em>(ω<em><sub>pc</sub></em>) = 1∠–180°, then the system</p>","options":[{"letter":"A","text":"<div> is stable</div>","isCorrect":false},{"letter":"B","text":"<div> is unstable</div>","isCorrect":false},{"letter":"C","text":"<div> is marginally stable</div>","isCorrect":true},{"letter":"D","text":"<div> has GM = 1 dB</div>","isCorrect":false}],"nat":{"low":"","high":""},"solution":"<p>(c)</p>\n<div> </div>\n<div><img src=\"/media/574068f31eb07c7b218e2286313128d73329631e.png\" loading=\"lazy\" /></div>","subject":"Technical"},{"qnum":15,"type":"MCQ","correct":"D","right":1,"wrong":0.33,"qtext":"<p>The block diagram of a control system is shown below :</p>\n<div> </div>\n<div><img src=\"/media/2b08219360bffa1d358367e569b